  "limitations": [
    "This draft binds the published RTX 5090 beta.5 image and source a87de3613c17bced777b446fb545f872d8395ec1. Both native beta.1 rows and their copied files are quarantined predecessor material, not current beta.2 execution or eligibility; both rows are preview and non-installable.",
    "The RTX 5090 published component reports a bit-identical same-path double build. No v0.16.0 reproducibility exception is renewed.",
    "The unmodified upstream OMP 18.15.0 client has no appliance commands. Its exact stock identities are recorded by qualification/client-components.json; source and asset-integrity reviews do not transfer platform or documented-route acceptance.",
    "RTX 5090 retains qwen38-5090-v0.13.0, configuration 751d22dc, 131072 context, 146368 BF16 KV tokens, DFlash2 K7, two requests plus two extra device-state slots and 180-second pending timeout; fit-dependent C2 is not a fairness guarantee.",
    "Native INT8 DFlash2 K7 serving shapes are retained targets, not completed beta.2 qualification: `Group64` A8 and FP32 head logits off, 131072 context, strict origin auth and sequential UUID-bound serving on port 18082. RTX 4090 is C1; RTX 3090 is C2 over one shared pool with a 350 W serving cap. No native vision, RTX 4090 C2 or smaller-host qualification.",
    "Schema 3 stores are release-isolated. A kept deployment-profile name does not establish cross-binary checkpoint compatibility; preserve predecessor stores and replay authoritative OMP transcripts.",
    "Strict origin auth requires a checkpoint root and a bearer key at least 32 bytes. Within one API-key principal prompt_cache_key is a session capability; use high-entropy unique keys and do not share the principal among mutually untrusted clients. MACs are not monotonic freshness.",
    "Checkpointing is best effort. Windows NTFS write-through is not POSIX fsync or a power-loss guarantee; finite export and victim-validation I/O can delay decode.",
    "No predecessor speed or restart-latency waiver transfers. The new RTX 5090 restore position 3 restore_0 TTFT failure is founder-waived only at 0.481856409 s candidate, 0.231568998 s incumbent and 0.481568998 s bound; raw failure and all other gates remain binding. The new RTX 4090 restore position 4 restore_1 cache-gap waiver remains pending exact-package evidence binding, at -52 candidate versus -48 incumbent.",
    "macOS remains manual-SSH preview; Linux client evidence is WSL2-scoped. Vision is RTX 5090 with macOS/Windows clients only. No multi-owner, multi-GPU, concurrent native-lane or silent cloud-fallback claim is added."
  ],
